14. **htop**: An interactive and colorful process viewer (requires installation).
15. **kill**: Sends a termination signal (SIGTERM) to gracefully stop a process using its PID.
16. **kill -9**: Forcefully terminates an unresponsive process immediately (SIGKILL).
17. **pkill**: Stops a running process using its name instead of the PID.
18. **jobs**: Lists active background jobs and their job IDs in the current shell session.
19. **bg %1**: Resumes a stopped background job and keeps it running in the background.
20. **fg %1**: Brings a background job back to the foreground terminal session.
   
